#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md
#: e6678166cbfa417994d7d2be977b644d
msgid ""
"Check GWexpy prerequisites, GPS-time assumptions, FFT conventions, and GWpy "
"compatibility before moving into tutorials, theory, or API pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:7
#: 63f1ff6aeedb4de5b8369dc5a78e5ded
msgid "Prerequisites and Conventions"
msgstr "前提条件と規約"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:9
#: 9915694645fb4c8facec2678d207173b
msgid ""
"This page is the entry point for the **shared prerequisites** and "
"**conventions** used across the GWexpy guides and tutorials. Page-specific "
"assumptions and mathematical details remain on their original pages; this "
"guide is meant to show where to check first."
msgstr ""
"このページは、GWexpy のガイドやチュートリアルを読む前に把握しておきたい**共通の前提条件**と**規約**をまとめたページです。 "
"個別アルゴリズムの仮定や数式の詳細は各ページに記載し、このページでは「どこを先に確認すべきか」を案内します。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:13
#: 7dbf04d886294124b7fe457dd0f2c7d3
msgid "1. Environment Prerequisites"
msgstr "1. 環境前提"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:15
#: 1933586152d24e37a3bf363f784e7223
msgid "The basic user-facing environment assumes **Python 3.11+**."
msgstr "基本的な利用環境は **Python 3.11 以上** を前提にしています。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:16
#: d830022d3dcf4de89524fdd0b5998793
msgid ""
"The minimum background is **basic Python**, **NumPy array handling**, and "
"optionally **Matplotlib**."
msgstr "最低限の前提知識は、**Python の基礎**、**NumPy 配列操作**、必要に応じて **Matplotlib** です。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:17
#: b82ac6ed93684de3b21cbf8ac6ed3c67
msgid ""
"Optional dependencies unlock additional features. See the [Installation "
"Guide](../tutorials/installation.md) for setup details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:19
#: 2edec52fd8264bd2a1b3f6cea8c47a0b
msgid ""
"If you want the shortest overall learning path first, start with [Getting "
"Started](../tutorials/getting_started.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:22
#: d2a29178f2524769a1c8bfab9fff633e
msgid "2. Data and Time Assumptions"
msgstr "2. データと時刻の前提"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:24
#: aa5f830e464040bca31484c32d1de5a6
msgid ""
"GWexpy is designed to stay compatible with `gwpy`-style time-series and "
"frequency-series containers."
msgstr "GWexpy は `gwpy` 系の時系列・周波数系列コンテナとの互換性を重視しています。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:25
#: 9a43e9ac54be45ebb18cb90752d221b3
msgid ""
"Some APIs assume **GPS time** explicitly. In particular, forecast timestamps"
" such as ARIMA outputs should not be confused with UTC-style time systems "
"that include leap seconds."
msgstr ""
"時刻の扱いでは **GPS 時刻** を前提とする API があります。特に ARIMA 予測時刻などは UTC の閏秒系と混同しないでください。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:26
#: a10be8233840404ea2c6f7e37c21ea33
msgid ""
"Some file formats do not preserve absolute timestamps. Audio formats are a "
"representative case where `t0=0.0` may be used only as a convenience "
"convention."
msgstr "ファイル形式によっては絶対時刻を保持しません。たとえば音声形式は `t0=0.0` を便宜的に使う場合があります。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:27
#: 134c54d901f148ca97802b6a8c7931cd
msgid ""
"Formats that only store local wall-clock time may require an explicit "
"`timezone`. A common example is GBD in the [File I/O Supported Formats "
"Guide](../how-to/io_formats.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:29
#: 839f1ccc06284f65a6276d4996aaf931
msgid ""
"For algorithm-specific assumptions, see [Validated "
"Algorithms](validated_algorithms.md)."
msgstr ""
"アルゴリズムごとの仮定まで確認したい場合は [検証済みアルゴリズム](validated_algorithms.md) を参照してください。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:32
#: e43812846eb34880a7bc631b3a38f496
msgid "3. FFT and Spectral Conventions"
msgstr "3. FFT とスペクトルの規約"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:34
#: e35aa239b2b94269beec571aea400efe
msgid ""
"GWexpy treats FFT **normalization**, **one-sided vs two-sided spectra**, and"
" **sign conventions** explicitly."
msgstr "GWexpy では、FFT の**正規化**、**片側/両側スペクトル**、**符号規約**を明示的に扱います。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:35
#: 4613affeb6a5446a8310f9d4e2d26347
msgid ""
"`fft_time` and `fft_space` follow different assumptions for target axes and "
"normalization."
msgstr "`fft_time` と `fft_space` では、対象軸と正規化の考え方が異なります。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:36
#: 889ed0f8cb3145eca51f9bc10f199c56
msgid ""
"`spectral_density` distinguishes PSD-style density from per-bin spectrum "
"values."
msgstr "`spectral_density` では PSD と spectrum の意味を区別して扱います。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:38
#: 8315770dfafc4a0fa10446b6678342dc
msgid ""
"For the mathematical details, see [FFT Specifications and "
"Conventions](../reference/index.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:41
#: 748488a9a61d43c6b0d0ff24d0c24257
msgid "4. GWpy Compatibility and GWexpy Extensions"
msgstr "4. GWpy 互換と GWexpy 拡張"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:43
#: 4f8a5db868e0410694c0f0cbf7d1d946
msgid ""
"GWexpy is built on top of GWpy and preserves the basic data model and "
"workflow expectations where possible."
msgstr "GWexpy は GWpy の上に構築されており、基本的なデータモデルと操作感を尊重しています。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:44
#: 73063f1ab21141c7a5f4f991623e6f03
msgid ""
"At the same time, it adds Matrix containers, the Field API, broader I/O "
"support, and extra analysis utilities that do not exist in GWpy."
msgstr "一方で、Matrix 系コンテナ、フィールド API、追加 I/O、解析ユーティリティなど GWpy にはない拡張があります。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:45
#: 675cbe73805549ce8317c106f0e8f320
msgid ""
"If you want a quick view of what is still \"GWpy-like\" and what is GWexpy-"
"specific, the migration guide is the fastest entry point."
msgstr "「GWpy と共通の仕様」と「GWexpy 固有の追加要素」を切り分けて確認したい場合は、移行ガイドを参照してください。"

#: ../../explanation/prerequisites_and_conventions.md:47
#: d9a7cefe81554c02b081e1546863d8fa
msgid ""
"For migration-oriented guidance, see [Migration from "
"GWpy](gwexpy_for_gwpy_users.md) and the [GWpy Difference API "
"Index](../reference/gwpy_added_api.md)."
msgstr ""

